    {
      "id": "dummy-west",
      "cardSha256": "ed9c2df4350546dd3fc20214b3b7eaf036d4503c01a27751bfeb1cc3d5bdb19e",
      "side": "russian",
      "name": "Dummy west",
      "idea": "The west face, W4 and W5, and the north-east tip Y3 hold only Dummies, three to a hex. The real force is the centre and the south-east: three squads in the centre, where nothing sees them, the HMG and the 9-2 at Y5, an MMG at Y4, the other MMG at X5, and an LMG at X3 and at X2 behind the Dummy face.",
      "givesUp": "W4, W5, and Y3 are not defended: Kampfgruppe Stahler may walk into the west face, and the Russians then hold exactly six hexes and can lose no other.",
      "terrain": [
        "The east face looks at the assault engineers' buildings: Y3, Y4, and Y5 see AA4 at range 2, Y4 and Y5 see AA5 at range 2, and Y5 and X5 see Y7 and Z6 at range 2.",
        "X4, the centre hex, has no LOS to or from any German setup Location, nor to any hex next to the building.",
        "Y5 sees thirteen German setup Locations (AA4, AA5, Y7, and Z6 at every level, and CC7), more than any other hex of the building.",
        "X3 is seen only from U3 and V2, and X2 from U3, V2, and T4; both stand one hex behind W4.",
        "Of the hexes held only by Dummies, W4 is seen from U3 and V2 at range 2, W5 from U3 at range 3 and from S5 and U8 at 4, and Y3 from AA4 at range 2, AA5 at 3, and CC3 at 4.",
        "The three plans of this card show the same number of counters in every hex of the Works (W4 3, W5 3, X2 2, X3 2, X4 4, X5 2, Y3 3, Y4 3, Y5 3), and every counter is a \"?\", so the Germans cannot tell from the stacks which plan was used. Each holds six hexes with real units and three with Dummies only; the plans differ in which three.",
        "The card makes X3 a Factory (SSR 5), which has no upper levels, so every counter stands at ground level, although the board's data gives the building levels 1 and 2.",
        "The side that Controls six of the building's nine hexes (W4, W5, X2, X3, X4, X5, Y3, Y4, Y5) at game end wins; the Russians Control all nine at the start."
      ],
